│   held back by others   Combination restrictions keep it shallower than its own
│                         failure point, so it cannot go deeper at the other
│                         cores' current offsets.
│ 
│   suspect               During a hunt: back at the offset it failed with, so
│                         this test tells whether it is part of the cause.
│ 
│   parked                During a hunt: held at an offset that passed before,
│                         usually 0, so it can't be the cause.
│ 
│   solo limit            The deepest offset a core passed with every other core
│                         at 0.
│ 
│   combination           Offsets that must not be reached together. A hunt may
│                         prove the group fails together, or leave an unresolved
│                         group restricted as a precaution.
│ 
│   lap                   One pass through the configured list of tests. A clean
│                         lap has passing evidence for each scheduled check at the
│                         resulting offsets. Only a full lap covers every required
│                         kind of load.
│ 
│   run                   One launch of one test. Confirming a solo limit, a hunt
│                         group or a deepening move needs several passes in a row.
│                         Ordinary lap steps can advance after one pass, while
│                         all-core steps also include repeated short runs and a
│                         long run.
│ 
│ 
│ The kinds of test
│   light load               One thread of light work, which lets a core boost
│                            highest.
│                            Like a game's main thread, opening apps or loading
│                            web pages.
│ 
█   heavy vector load        One thread of heavy vector math, which draws the most
█                            current.
█                            Like video encoding, 3D rendering or scientific math
█                            on one thread.
█ 
█   load steps               A load switched on and off in bursts, so the voltage
█                            has to follow sudden swings.
█                            Like a game loading a level, or apps waking up for
█                            short tasks.
█ 
█   partial load             A load that runs only part of the time.
█                            Like background work: a video call, music playback, a
█                            download.
█ 
█   both threads             Work on both threads of a core at once.
█                            Like compiling or other work that keeps both threads
█                            of a core busy.
█ 
█   idle with short bursts   The machine mostly idle, with short bursts, the way
█                            it sits on a desktop.
█                            Like a desktop left alone, or reading and typing.
█ 
█   all-core load            Heavy work on many cores at once, for power and heat.
█                            Like rendering, compiling or exporting video on every
█                            core.
█ 
█ 
█ Passing tests can't prove offsets will never fail. They show which tests passed, and more laps catch rarer failures.

